<title>BANGLADESH: Trading on Dhaka bourse threatened by protest.</title>
<headline>Trading on Dhaka bourse threatened by protest.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading on the Dhaka Stock Exchange (DSE) faced uncertainty as hundreds of traders on the unofficial kerb market threatened to shut down the bourse, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;If trading takes place, the share prices will go down further,&quot; one broker said. The kerb market traders on Tuesday warned that they would stop transactions on the floor unless the government removed Finance Minister A.A.M.S. Kibria and took steps to check falling prices.</p>
<p>The market was closed on Wednesday for public holiday. The DSE benchmark index closed 78.57 points or 6.81 percent down at 1,074.95 on Tuesday. -- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
